course: dictionary
lesson: 770
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Bearcat is a noun with three meanings, so you need the clues in the sentence to know which one the writer means.
explain: «The binturong, or bearcat, is an Asian tree animal with a gripping tail.» The sentence tells you bearcat is another name for the binturong, an animal from Asia. Its name sounds like a mix of a bear and a cat, but the sentence shows it is neither.
explain: Names can mislead. A name can make you guess wrongly, so always check the clues. Ask: does my meaning fit the sentence? If it does not, look at the words around the word again.
explain: Some words have special meanings in some places or groups. In old US informal speech, a bearcat is a strong, fierce or very lively person, and some US sports teams are named the Bearcats.
fact: One word can have more than one meaning, so check the context to find the right one.
fact: The bearcat is a binturong, a furry animal from the forests of South and Southeast Asia.
fact: The bearcat is neither a bear nor a cat, even though its name suggests both.
fact: «Bearcat» can also mean the red panda, or, in old US informal use, a strong, fierce or very lively person.
fact: Bearcats are said to smell like buttered popcorn, and they are related to civets.
exercise: «The binturong, or bearcat, lives in the forests of South and Southeast Asia.» What is a bearcat in this sentence? | A kind of cat from Africa | A sports team player | A big brown bear from Europe | *A furry animal with a gripping tail
exercise: Coach Lee shouts, «Our goalkeeper is a real bearcat!» What does the coach mean? | A red panda asleep in a tree | A furry animal from Asian forests | A bear that is hungry | *A strong, fierce and very lively person
exercise: Why is the name bearcat misleading? | It is a bear that loves popcorn | It is a cat with a bear's voice | *It is neither a bear nor a cat | It only lives in the sea
test: «Some people also call the red panda a bearcat.» What does this tell you? | Red pandas are a kind of bear | Nobody ever uses the word bearcat | Bearcat always means a red panda | *Bearcat can mean another animal, the red panda
test: Why should you check the clues in a sentence before deciding what a word means? | Because long words are always harder | *Because one word can have more than one meaning | Because all words mean the same thing | Because the dictionary is always wrong
exam: Sami reads, «Bearcats are said to smell like buttered popcorn.» What should Sami do to be sure which meaning of bearcat is used? | *Read the words around it and check which meaning fits | Guess that it means a bear | Skip the word and never come back to it | Look only at the first letter of the word
